  "notes": [
    "Official OECD enlargement page: '38 Members today'; accession discussions underway with eight countries (Argentina, Brazil, Bulgaria, Croatia, Indonesia, Peru, Romania, Thailand). Last accession: Costa Rica, 25 May 2021.",
    "No new member joined in 2025-2026 as of 2026-11-16. Romania was expected to receive an invitation in 2026 (Cormann, March 2026) but as of Oct 2026 it was still pending; re-check if updating later. Bulgaria/Croatia/Peru also target 2026-2027.",
    "Argentina's process was slowed in 2023-2024 but remains formally open on the OECD list.",
    "Taiwan is not a member; participates in some committees (e.g. Competition, Steel) as an observer under the name 'Chinese Taipei' - not listed as these are committee-level arrangements."
